===Etymology 2===
Medieval Latin, introduced in the 12th century by [[w:Gherardo of Cremona|Gherardo of Cremona]] as a translation of {{etyl|ar|la}} {{term|جيب|tr=jiba|lang=ar||chord}} (ultimately a loan from {{etyl|sa|la}} {{term|ज्या|tr=jyā|lang=sa||bowstring}}) by confusion with {{term|جيب|tr=jaib|lang=ar||bosom, fold in a garment}}.

====Noun====
{{la-noun|sinus|sinus|sinūs|m|fourth}}

# {{context|mathematics|lang=la}} [[chord]] of an arc, [[sine]]

